menu "app_cfg -- device configuration"

config APP_CFG_NAMESPACE
    string "NVS namespace for application configuration"
    default "appcfg"
    help
        Every persistent setting the template owns lives in this one namespace, so a
        factory reset has a single, auditable definition.

config APP_CFG_PERSIST_PARTITION
    string "NVS partition for data that survives a factory reset"
    default "persist"
    help
        Label of a second NVS partition, opened with app_cfg_persist_open(). A factory
        reset, Wi-Fi provisioning (tools/provision_nvs.sh, which rewrites the main nvs
        partition) and /api/forget leave it alone, so it is the place for anything that
        must never go backwards: a monotonic counter, a network join nonce, a pairing.

config APP_CFG_AP_PASS_SALT
    string "SoftAP passphrase salt"
    default "esp32-lorawan-node"
    help
        Mixed with the device MAC to derive the provisioning AP passphrase. The default
        is public, so anyone can compute any device's passphrase from the MAC its SSID
        advertises. Set your own in sdkconfig.local, which git ignores:
            CONFIG_APP_CFG_AP_PASS_SALT="<random string>"

config APP_CFG_AP_PASS_FIXED
    string "Fixed SoftAP passphrase (empty = derive per device)"
    default ""
    help
        Leave empty in anything you ship. A fixed passphrase is convenient on a bench
        where you provision the same board repeatedly and would rather not read the
        boot log every time.

endmenu
